<title>CANADA: Canada's Goodale to announce CWB changes Friday.</title>
<headline>Canada's Goodale to announce CWB changes Friday.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Agriculture Minister Ralph Goodale plans to announce changes to the Canadian Wheat Board and the way Prairie grains and oilseeds are exported at a press briefing Friday, an Agriculture Canada statement said.</p>
<p>Goodale plans to make his intentions public at a conference in his electoral constituency of Regina, the capital of Saskatchewan, at 1200 EDT/1600 GMT.</p>
<p>A federal export panel appointed by Goodale last December suggested removing feed barley from the CWB export monopoly, allowing farmers to sell up to a quarter of the milling wheat crop on a CWB spot market and altering the CWB's governance.</p>
<p>-- Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548</p>
</text>
